// Result is the conventional explicit success-or-error variant. It owns no
// storage beyond its inline discriminator and payload. The first alternative
// is the zero value, so a default-initialized Result is always an error.
// Draft specification: section 5, "Variants, Option, and Result".
package result

pub Result[T: type, E: type] :: variant {
    err: E,
    ok: T,
}
